    "findings": [
      "The VSM cost comparison retains the same sixteen-region projected grid, five relevant pages, and highlights three changed pages in the right view. Static reuse and invalidation are labelled separately; the text explicitly excludes solving all indirect light.",
      "The low-input/high-output reconstruction model reveals the connecting arrow and corresponding orange object on the projected grids. It does not claim every output lighting sample is newly calculated.",
      "TSR and DLSS SR are compared by role with distinct teal/orange paths and explicit implementation/hardware qualifications, rather than claiming equal implementation or equal quality.",
      "The 4x4=16 versus 2x2=4 projected grids show half width times half height equals one-quarter internal pixels. The remaining geometry, shadow, reconstruction and other work is labelled. The final-frame cost is explicitly distinguished from this pixel-count ratio.",
      "Frames912/1730/2771 retain the preceding model and frames913/1731/2772 start the next model exactly. All sampled images preserve clean black sources without baked narration captions; labels are readable and projected top/front/side faces remain visible."
